# AI Content Serving

**Rule:** Pages intended for AI consumption (transparency, FAQ, methodology, for-ai, protocol-adopters, etc.) must serve **clean room HTML**, not full HTML.

- **Clean room HTML:** Minimal, self-contained HTML. Inline CSS. No React SPA. No external scripts. No Cloudflare Browser Rendering. Same pattern as `serve-bot-list-html`, `serve-bot-state-html`, `serve-bot-agent-html`.
- **Full HTML (forbidden for AI pages):** React SPA shell, browser-rendered snapshot, or any HTML that requires JS to display content.

**Implementation:** Route AI pages through `/api/serve-clean-html` → Supabase Edge Functions (`serve-bot-content-html`, etc.). Never let AI pages fall through to `/_spa.html` or `serve-bot-static-html` (Cloudflare Browser Rendering).
